if you've been thinking about buying a  new iphone stop right there in your  tracks do not do it because we're gonna  be getting the new iphone 14 lineup in  less than one month yes it was just  confirmed by mark german the most  reliable apple leaker that apple  september event is happening on  september 7th which is a wednesday and  yes they always release their new  iphones on that day and even better he  says that we're actually gonna have the  iphone 14 models in our hands on  september 16th yes less than a month  from today and i recommend waiting  because those new iphone 14s especially  the 14 pro models are going to be  absolutely insane there's going to be  some  crazy revolutions like in the camera  department as well as others with some  new features that we've never had on the  iphone that android has had for many  years and not only that but this year  there are going to be even more features  that are going to be exclusive to the  iphone 14 pro and there's one that i  really want to focus on it's something  that's going to fix an issue that has  been plaguing the iphones for years  especially since the iphone 12 and even  this 13  model so before i get into explaining  that i've got to go through some of the  contacts first of all the iphone 14 pro  is gonna get the a16 chip compared to  the standard iphone 14 models retaining  the a15 so yes it's gonna have even more  performance than it already has now we  did get a report this morning saying  that tsmc is starting their three  nanometer chip production for the m2 pro  and then the future a17 for the iphone  15 next year but what that means is that  the current iphone 14 pro that we're  about to get in less than a month is  going to be sticking to the a16 which  unfortunately according to shrimp apple  pro a leaker on twitter he says that the  a16 bionic is gonna continue to use the  same five nanometer from tsmc's n5p yes  that's exactly what we already have on  the a15 bionic and it is going to be  offering slightly better cpu performance  faster ram and a better gpu but there is  a very big problem with this the iphone  13 pro with the a15 chip especially with  the 5 core gpu model it suffers from  thermal throttling that is lowering the  performance as you can see right here in  geekbench performance charts you have  the apple a15 bionic right here in the  iphone 13 and the iphone 13 mini and  they score around 11  200 points which is crazy crazy fast  that's in terms of metal graphics but  take a look at this the apple a14 bionic  yes that's the last generation chip is  actually faster and that's with the same  four core gpu 12  425 yes the previous gen a14 faster than  the new a15 in the iphone 13 and the  reason for that is thermal throttling  due to the lack of a decent cooling  solution yes these iphones use passive  cooling just like the ipad except the  ipad is larger so it's able to dissipate  the heat across the larger tablet  compared to the smaller iphone which  heats up faster and because of that  apple literally caps the performance of  that chip down lower quite a bit lower  than the a14 now if you look at the a15  bionic chip in the iphone 13 pro those  do score higher because they have a five  core gpu however it's not much faster  than the four core version and then if  you split that up into performance per  core the a14 in the ipad air is getting  more performance per core and that's of  course because the iphone just can't  handle the heat the cooling solution  sucks well thankfully apple is working  on a solution to this problem and it's  why i think these new iphone 14 pro  models are gonna be incredibly good in  terms of everyday reliability and  performance as well yes apple has been  aggressively testing vapor chamber  cooling solutions for the 2022 iphones  yes that's finally this year and that is  going to allow them to really unlock the  performance of the a16 ship now if you  don't know how that works there are some  other phones that actually already have  vapor chamber cooling and as you can see  right here this is a copper vapor  chamber cooler and what happens is at  the source of the heat whereas where the  chip is it heats up and hot air moves  around sort of in this loop where it  goes to a different location and it  comes back around a little bit colder  than it was before and it just cycles  around like this allowing the chip to  stay cooler sort of like a radiator in  an engine so if this year apple  engineers a well-designed vapor chamber  cooler for the iphone 14 pro and pro max  models that literally by itself could  lead to a huge performance boost  compared to what we have right now with  the iphone 13 models because we have  just so much performance that is locked  behind the overheating so literally with  the same a15 chip that we already have  we could get a big performance boost and  because of that it kind of makes sense  for why apple is sticking to the n5p  five nanometer process node on the a16  chip because if they improve the cooling  that's gonna do a lot of the performance  work for them by unlocking the extra  performance which means they won't have  to do that much tweaking to the a16 ship  at all they just have to tweak it a  little bit and it'll look like it's a  new awesome super fast chip but really  it was the cooling that did most of the  work so apple has a huge advantage and  opportunity this year by adding a vapor  chamber cooler now on top of that we are  going to be getting a new 5g chip that's  going to be cooler it's going to be the  snapdragon 865 which is using the six  nanometer process which is more  efficient than the x60 that they're  using right now and that's gonna lead to  less heat and of course better battery  life as well so we'll have less display  dimming issues because the display  dimming issue was huge with the iphone  12 it got better with the iphone 13 but  it's still around and it's still very  annoying so that vapor chamber cooling  along with the new 5g chip that could  mean that we'll finally get rid of the  display dimming issues on the iphone 14  pro and pro max now not only that but we  are expecting even more awesome  exclusive features with the 14 pro and  pro max model first of all we're getting  taller displays and as you can see we're  finally getting rid of the notch you  have the pro max right here in the pro  they have this new pill shaped and  single hole punch cutouts that look a  lot better than the old notched version  not only that but we get a really slim  and sleek speaker grille and the bezels  themselves look thinner not only that  but the pro models are getting the new  48 megapixel camera system which i think  is going to record 8k video at 60 fps  that's going to be exclusive to the 14  pro models not only that but we're also  getting the always on display feature on  the pro models because they're going to  have new display panels that can go down  to one hertz refresh rate finally giving  us a feature that's been around on  android for many many years and the  regular iphone 14 is not getting that  and even better we might even get 256  gigs of base storage with the 14 pro  alongside the rumored price increase  which might be around 100 more expensive  than it is right now for the 13 pro and  the pro max model so with that said  apple has some huge opportunities this  year to make the iphone 14 pro a lot  better with the vapor chamber cooler and  all of those other features and because  of that i strongly believe that you  should not be buying any iphone model  right now you should be waiting until  apple's september 7th event because i  think you'll be blown away by the new  features we're getting in the iphone 14  lineup now if you totally disagree with  my thoughts let me know down in the  comment section below but if you like  this video click the circle button  subscribe and check out one of those two  right over there thanks for watching and  we'll see you in the next video  [Music]

